    {
      "id": "bool",
      "name": "bool",
      "category": "MeshWindingNumberGrid",
      "signature": "bool(Target, Cancel F)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TMeshWindingNumberGrid*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel F",
          "type": ")>",
          "default": "[]("
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TFunction<",
      "docs": "Sample mesh winding number (MWN) on a discrete grid. Can sample full grid, or\ncompute MWN values along a specific iso-contour and then fill in rest of grid\nwith correctly-signed values via fast sweeping (this is the default)\nTODO:\n- I think we are over-exploring the grid most of the time. eg along an x-ray that\nintersects the surface, we only need at most 2 cells, but we are computing at least 3,\nand possibly 5.\n- it may be better to use something like bloomenthal polygonizer continuation? where we\nare keeping track of active edges instead of active cells?"
    },
